From d6dd85b073952a040bee27d8ed855dee63f8038b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:31:03 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] zgx: text below 2x is drawn for the screen's subpixels, as
 ClearType draws it

Zeron's text on a ~96 dpi Windows screen read blurry beside Windows' own:
greyscale coverage leaves each stem over two columns at part strength
(Geist hints vertically only), which zgx#1516's whole-pixel places and
firmed edges can't do better. Windows' text is sharp because ClearType
covers each subpixel apart.

apps/zgx's zgx moves to hoangvu12/zgx 998140e69 (branch
nightly-lcd-998140e6): main's pin, zeronsh/zgx b9e744ddd, with one commit
on it. Glyphs keyed CacheKeyFlags::LCD are swash subpixel masks, drawn by a
dual-source pipeline (Shading::Lcd) that blends each channel by its own
coverage. Only into an opaque window's own target, below 2x, off macOS, on
a device with dual-source blending: frosted or transparent windows and
isolated layers keep greyscale, since their pixels are blended again. The
desktop host follows Windows' ClearType setting (on, RGB or BGR) and reads
it again on a settings change; ZGX_LCD_TEXT=0, rgb or bgr overrides it.

Only the zgx pin and the lockfile's sources change here.
